An ID selector styles a specific element with a unique identifier, defined with a # followed by the element's ID. Example:
#header {
  color: blue;
  font-size: 20px;
}

Function declaration:
function greet(name) { return "Hello, " + name; }

Arrow function:
const greet = (name) => { return "Hello, " + name; }

Use if to check a condition, else for the alternative, and else if for additional conditions; use switch to check a value against multiple cases. Example:
if (x > 10) { console.log("x > 10"); }
else if (x === 10) { console.log("x = 10"); }
else { console.log("x < 10"); }

